==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequiredEverywhere  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AuthRequiredEverywhere.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the model to produce a world where an unauthenticated Operation has outcome=Success, directly violating the authentication-boundary invariant in FR-001.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired, ValidationBeforeMutation
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)
      - ValidationBeforeMutation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ClosedTaskRule  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_ClosedTaskRule.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a PATCH operation on a Done task with KeepsDone intent to succeed, violating the closed-task edit rule (FR-011 / 409 task_closed).
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule
      - FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets the model produce two DeletionLog entries pointing to the same task, violating the append-only / no-duplicate invariant that protects the deletion audit trail.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_018_DeletionLogged
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_DeletionLogged: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeletionLogCompleteness  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeletionLogCompleteness.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a DeletionLog entry whose deletedBy member does not match any successful DeleteTask operation caller, breaking attribution correctness and audit completeness.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, AttributionCorrectness, FR_012_PermanentDeletion, FR_018_DeletionLogged
      - AuditCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_PermanentDeletion: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_DeletionLogged: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Removing the permission matrix fact lets the Allowed relation be arbitrary, which can produce a world where Unauth has a permitted operation or AuthMember is missing a permission — violating both LeastPrivilege and PermissionCompleteness.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, PermissionCompleteness, FR_004_FlatPermissions
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - PermissionCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_FlatPermissions: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeleteProducesLog  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeleteProducesLog.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a successful DeleteTask operation with no corresponding DeletionLog entry, meaning deletions can go unlogged and violating FR-018's audit-log requirement.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_018_DeletionLogged
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_DeletionLogged: FAIL (expected)

